{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit limits and return rules","requirement":"A lessor may not require a security deposit above one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% annual interest, provide receipts and a condition statement, and return the deposit with an itemized deduction list within 30 days after tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Residential real property leases and tenancies; applies to lessors and their agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"residential real property"},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest deposit transfer liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"If the lessor fails to deposit, transfer, or return the deposit, the tenant may recover three times the deposit plus 5% interest, court costs, and attorney's fees; the lessor forfeits the right to retain the deposit for listed violations.","effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2)","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts upfront charges and fee-in-lieu-of-deposit cap","requirement":"A lessor or agent may not require upfront payments beyond first month's rent, last month's rent, a one-month security deposit, and key and lock costs; a fee in lieu of a deposit must be optional and cannot exceed one month's rent.","key_value":"first + last month's rent; 1 month deposit; key/lock; fee-in-lieu max 1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies at or prior to commencement; applies to lessors and their agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"residential tenancy"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and,\n(ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,\n(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu screening restriction","requirement":"A lessor offering a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every approved applicant regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, household size, or credit score, and may not use those factors to set the fee.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies to lessors who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit to approved applicants for residential occupancy.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"fee in lieu of security deposit"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(E) require a lessor who offers such a fee in lieu of security deposit:  (I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;  and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
